title: Docs should focus on easy ad-hoc use, not heavily expose the full c2c swarm/infrastructure
---
Current docs and skills lean heavily into the swarm multi-agent topology (rooms, coordinators, managed sessions, push delivery, hooks, relay). For most users — especially first-time adopters — the value proposition is simple: send/receive messages between agents. Docs should lead with ad-hoc use cases (send a message, check inbox, run a monitor) and keep swarm infrastructure as an advanced/secondary topic. Don't scare newcomers with the full complexity upfront. Focus: install, init, send, monitor, done.